WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:01.750
OK.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:06.519
This is this is a sort of a complicated thing
to discuss.

00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:11.830
But at some point, we, meaning the United
States collectively, we're going to owe the

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.900
world an explanation and an apology.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:19.119
And I don't mean just generally for Donald
Trump, but I'm talking more broadly because

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.910
of our failure on Corona virus.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.880
I'm talking broadly because of our failure
to continue leading on climate change.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:30.839
I'm talking about our failure really to just
hold back the advancement of humanity, instead

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:35.840
regressing dramatically over the last three
and a half years and maybe for another four

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.980
now to set the stage accurately.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:45.940
I'm not pretending that the United States
nor the world were idealist panaceas during

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.550
the era of Barack Obama.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.080
That would be revisionist history.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.170
That would be wrong.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:54.400
That's certainly not the point of the segment
to pretend things were just perfect until

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.970
Donald Trump became president.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:01:01.570
But as an example, we were at least an important
part of thinking about how to deal with climate

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:04.340
change when Barack Obama was president of
the United States.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:09.090
We hadn't figured it out, certainly, but we
were serious participants in the conversation.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:14.400
The Obama administration understood the U.S.
is disproportionately relative to our population,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:20.249
a big polluter, a big emitter of of of pollution
and emissions.

00:01:20.249 --> 00:01:22.499
And we were taking it seriously.

00:01:22.499 --> 00:01:23.890
Not enough was done.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:29.590
We had not figured it out, but our role was
at least respectable around the world.

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:36.200
Our role now on climate change has gone from
respectable to not respectable to having no

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.540
role whatsoever because we're actually a huge
part of the problem.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:43.939
As Donald Trump has claimed, that climate
change is a hoax created by China, propped

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:46.950
up oil and gas while loosening car emission
standards.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.659
And the world has rightly started either.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:53.659
Ignoring us in these important climate change
conversations are actually pointing out that

00:01:53.659 --> 00:01:56.390
we're a huge part of the problem on Corona.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:01.250
Of course, this administration has proven
that it still matters who is president.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.859
We have seen arguably one of the worst responses
in the world to the pandemic.

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:08.660
I don't know how much time I have to spend
on that today since we've covered it almost

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.020
daily for months.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:15.830
But suffice it to say, almost any functioning
adult would have said, I don't need to lead

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.840
this, let's defer to the doctors and we'd
be better off.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:19.840
Right.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.400
We didn't need anything outlandish to better
handle corona virus than the way this administration

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.400
has handled it.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:31.160
We just needed some adult to say, oh, I'm
not an expert in this, but I know who is.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.090
Let's let let let let's allow them to lead
the way.

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:40.500
We've talked about voting Trump out as only
being the first step.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.650
And that's true from a policy standpoint,
but it's also true from the standpoint of

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.500
defeating Trump ism.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.510
Defeating Trump will not instantly end Trump
ism.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.630
If Donald Trump loses in November and leaves
the Oval Office in January.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.300
But there is another area in which defeating
Donald Trump is only the first step, which

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:05.330
is starting to rebuild our alliances around
the world, starting to recover some semblance

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:09.270
of respect from our historical allies and
from the people of this planet.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:14.290
So this is not about being ashamed of the
country, even though certainly you wouldn't

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.900
be wrong to feel that right now as we have
become a laughingstock.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:23.720
This is not about punishing Trump supporters,
although there's no doubt that they are responsible

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.190
for the fact that this president was elected.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:32.560
This is about realizing that part of being
respected again and rebuilding those relationships

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:40.310
is going to be an implicit apology, some kind
of explanation as to our commitment to fixing

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:45.170
the disaster that the United States has been
globally during the time of Donald Trump.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:51.050
Now, if Donald Trump were to win in November,
the case for such an apology and an explanation

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:54.980
and a rehabilitation of our reputation becomes
much more difficult.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.380
Almost 63 million people voted for Donald
Trump in 2016.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.790
The reality is some number close to that or
even more are going to vote for him again

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.010
in 2020.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:11.580
The question, of course, is going to be do
enough additional people vote for Joe Biden

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.320
such that Donald Trump loses in the Electoral
College?

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.909
Now, in the next segment, I'm going to talk
about the reality that any view that thinks

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:19.909
Biden's got.

00:04:19.909 --> 00:04:20.910
This is not based.

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:24.440
In fact, I'm going to go into detail about
that after the break.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:29.800
But let's imagine, even if Donald Trump is
defeated in November, there will still be

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:36.099
the inconvenient and humiliating reality that
somewhere between probably 60 and 65 million

00:04:36.099 --> 00:04:42.069
Americans in all likelihood, will have seen
the last four years of Trump and the disaster

00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:43.069
that it's been.

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:46.951
And they will say, I'm voting for another
four and they will vote.

00:04:46.951 --> 00:04:49.009
For Donald Trump, a second time.

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:51.050
So how do we get out of this?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:56.879
Removing Donald Trump is only going to be
step zero point one in the process.

00:04:56.879 --> 00:04:58.560
The world deserves answers.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.969
The world deserves an explanation.

00:04:59.969 --> 00:05:06.590
We owe it to the world and an explanation
about how we will not allow the country to

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:12.419
be hijacked by the non-thinking ideas of the
60 plus million people who, even if Trump

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:17.430
loses in November, will have voted for another
four years.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:18.909
So what is the path forward?

00:05:18.909 --> 00:05:20.849
I actually don't have the answers.

00:05:20.849 --> 00:05:22.319
I want to hear from you.

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:24.460
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:06:57.589
We'll take a break and we'll follow up about
this either tomorrow or next week.

